# STAGE B — only after Stage A is deployed/proven and declared as the rollback floor.
# Do NOT keep V22-V26 safety metadata under outer version=2.
# Recommended shape:
#
#   LEGACY_STATE_VERSION = 2
#   STATE_VERSION = 3
#
# New loader:
#   - accepts version 2 as legacy input, with replay/provider-intent evidence
#     treated as unavailable (exact legacy retry remains fail-closed where needed);
#   - accepts version 3 with the full V12..V26 replay/intent schema;
#   - writes version 3 only.
#
# Stage-A binaries accept only v2. Once a v3 file exists they set
# persistence_blocked and, because Stage A gates provider entry, return 503 before
# any Notion call. This is the intended safe rollback behavior.
#
# Release metadata must record:
#   minimum_safe_rollback_commit = <exact Stage-A commit>
# and deployment/rollback tooling must refuse rollback below it after the first
# successful v3 publication. Older pre-floor binaries are NOT safe rollback
# targets because the exact current server treats persistence failure as an
# optimization miss and can re-enter the provider.
